.\" Man page for freshen, generated and kept in sync with the CLI by hand.
.\" Run `freshen man` to print this page, or `man -l crates/freshen/man/freshen.1`.
.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt FRESHEN 1
.Os freshen
.Sh NAME
freshen \- keep a developer machine up to date
.Sh SYNOPSIS
freshen [options]
freshen man
freshen completions {zsh|bash|fish|powershell}
freshen logs
freshen history
freshen self-update
freshen schedule install [--every HOURS]
freshen schedule remove
.Sh DESCRIPTION
freshen upgrades the package managers, language toolchains and containers on a
developer machine.  It detects the tools that are installed, reports what is
outdated, performs the upgrades and prints a summary.  It runs on macOS,
Linux and Windows.

By default freshen runs every step it detects.  A step that is not installed is
skipped.  Use --only or --skip to restrict the run, and --check to report
outdated items without changing anything.

The configuration file is optional.  On macOS and Linux it is read from
~/.config/freshen/config.toml, on Windows from %APPDATA%\\freshen\\config.toml.
The --config option overrides the default location.
.Sh OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
Show what would run without changing anything.
.TP
.B --doctor
Verify the environment (tools found, permissions, config validity) and print
actionable fixes without changing anything.
.TP
.B --verbose
Print more detail about what freshen is doing, including diagnostic lines.
Mutually exclusive with --quiet.
.TP
.B --quiet
Print less: suppress informational progress lines, keeping only errors.
Mutually exclusive with --verbose.
.TP
.B --check
Report outdated items without changing anything; exit 2 when updates are pending.
.TP
.B --list-steps
List every known step, whether it was detected and why it would be skipped.
.TP
.B --json
Print the report as JSON instead of the plain-text summary. Mutually exclusive
with --markdown.
.TP
.B --markdown
Print the report as Markdown instead of the plain-text summary. Mutually
exclusive with --json.
.TP
.B --config PATH
Read the configuration from this file instead of the default location.
.TP
.B --container-runtime RUNTIME
Use this container runtime instead of detecting the active one (colima,
orbstack, docker-desktop, podman-desktop, rancher-desktop, podman, docker).
.TP
.B --only STEP
Only run the named steps (comma-separated, repeatable).
.TP
.B --skip STEP
Skip the named steps (comma-separated, repeatable).
.TP
.B --profile PROFILE
Run the steps enabled by the named profile, defined in the configuration file.
.TP
.B --except PACKAGE
Exclude these Chocolatey packages from the upgrade (repeatable,
comma-separated). Chocolatey only runs on Windows.
.TP
.B --yes, \-y
Assume yes for every confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B --force-kill
Force-kill applications that do not quit gracefully.
.TP
.B --cleanup
Run destructive cleanup (cache, old-version and image pruning). Aliases:
--allow-cleanup, --destructive-cleanup.
.TP
.B --prune-report
Report the reclaimable space from each cleanup step's dry-run listing without
removing anything.
.TP
.B --install-macos-updates
Install the macOS system updates instead of only reporting them (macOS only).
.TP
.B --install-firmware-updates
Install the available firmware updates instead of only reporting them
(Linux only).
.TP
.B --install-wsl-updates
Install the WSL kernel update with \fBwsl --update\fR instead of only
reporting that it is available (Windows only).
.TP
.B --install-nvim-lazy
Sync lazy.nvim plugins instead of only reporting that the sync is available.
.TP
.B --install-nvim-packer
Sync packer.nvim plugins instead of only reporting that the sync is available.
.TP
.B --install-nvim-mason
Update Mason packages instead of only reporting that the update is available.
.TP
.B --install-nvim-treesitter
Update Treesitter parsers instead of only reporting that the update is available.
.TP
.B --wsl-distro DISTRO
Run the Linux package-manager steps inside this WSL distribution on Windows.
.TP
.B --restart-services
Restart the services that need a restart after a step, restoring their previous
enabled/running state on error or interrupt (Linux only).
.TP
.B --restart-apps
Restart the desktop applications that were stopped before an upgrade, reusing
the recorded snapshot of what was stopped (Linux only).
.TP
.B --bump
Replace \fBlts\fR/\fBlatest\fR mise tool requests with a fixed version when
upgrading mise-managed tools (opt-in, off by default).
.TP
.B --docker-bump
Pull pinned container images too (opt-in, off by default).
.TP
.B --prune-unused-older-than DAYS
Prune dangling container images that have not been used for N days (only runs
with --cleanup, opt-in, off by default).
.TP
.B --reinstall-go
Reinstall outdated \fBgo install\fR binaries instead of only reporting them
(opt-in, off by default).
.TP
.B --install-aws-cli-updates
Update AWS CLI v2 through the official installer instead of only reporting that
a newer version is available (opt-in, off by default).
.TP
.B --trust-config
Trust every hook and custom step from the configuration file without
prompting, recording their hashes in the trust store next to the configuration
file. Without this flag a new or changed hook or custom step requires an
interactive confirmation before it runs, and a non-interactive run refuses it.
.TP
.B --snapshot-retention COUNT
Keep this many pre-upgrade snapshot files (0 keeps every snapshot, default 10).
.TP
.B --step-timeout SECONDS
Stop a single step after this many seconds (0 disables the timeout, default 0).
.TP
.B --timeout SECONDS
Stop the whole run after this many seconds (0 disables the timeout, default 0).
.TP
.B --jobs N
How many read-only checks --check may query at the same time (default 4).
.TP
.B --skip-network-check [true|false]
Skip the preflight check that the network is reachable.
.TP
.B --skip-disk-check [true|false]
Skip the preflight check that enough disk space is free.
.TP
.B --skip-battery-check [true|false]
Skip the preflight check that the battery is not too low.
.TP
.B --skip-metered-check [true|false]
Skip the preflight check for a metered connection or hotspot.
.TP
.B --skip-package-manager-check [true|false]
Skip the check for another package manager process.
.TP
.B --package-manager-wait SECONDS
Seconds to wait for another package manager to finish before aborting
(default 30).
.TP
.B --min-free-disk-gib GIB
Minimum free disk space in GiB required before updating (default 1).
.TP
.B --battery-threshold PERCENT
Battery percentage below which an update on battery is refused (default 20).
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B man
Print this man page.
.TP
.B completions {zsh|bash|fish|powershell}
Print a shell completion script for the given shell.
.TP
.B logs
Show the log of the last freshen run.
.TP
.B history
List previous runs and what each one changed, from the snapshots.
.TP
.B self-update
Upgrade freshen itself through the package manager that installed it. When
Homebrew owns the installation, \fBbrew upgrade freshen\fR is run.
.TP
.B schedule install [--every HOURS]
Install (write and load) a launchd agent that runs \fBfreshen --check\fR
every \fIHOURS\fR hours (default 24) on macOS.
.TP
.B schedule remove
Unload and delete the scheduled launchd agent on macOS.
.Sh EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success: every step succeeded or was skipped.
.TP
.B 1
A step failed or timed out (also used for startup errors).
.TP
.B 2
Updates are pending (--check).
.TP
.B 3
A preflight or package-manager check failed.
.TP
.B 130
The run was interrupted.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
freshen reads an optional TOML configuration file.  On macOS and Linux the
default path is ~/.config/freshen/config.toml; on Windows it is
%APPDATA%\\freshen\\config.toml.  Command-line flags win over values in the
configuration file, and the configuration file wins over built-in defaults.
.Sh FILES
~/.config/freshen/config.toml  configuration file on macOS and Linux
%APPDATA%\\freshen\\config.toml  configuration file on Windows
.Sh SEE ALSO
The freshen README and documentation: https://github.com/yildirimarda/freshen
.Sh AUTHOR
Written by the freshen project.
